WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.360
Satoshi, who defeated
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.860
...and claimed victory
in the Masters Tournament...

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.820
And Go, who managed to meet Mew again
through Project Mew...

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.000
Okido Laboratory, Kanto Region

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.000
These two have returned
to their usual lives.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.500
We did it, guys!

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.300
You battled marvelously, Satoshi.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.390
Professor Okido!

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.720
Allow me to recite a poem...

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.270
You set off from here
And to here you have returned,
Now reigning supreme

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.230
Couldn’t have done it
without Pikachu and the rest!

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.320
Indeed.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.400
Keep that modesty
and you’ll surely keep on improving.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.240
Right!

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.410
I get the feeling you won’t be
visiting us again for quite some time.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.530
Mom! How could you tell?

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.870
Why, because I’m your mother.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:00.620
I tend to have a pretty good idea
what my own son is thinking.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:01.830
Here, your lunch.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:02.630
Thanks!

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.300
Then I’ll be going!

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.550
Have a good trip!

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.090
Give my regards to
Sakuragi and the others.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.010
Right!

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.680
You guys! We won’t get to see each other for a while,
so everyone take care!

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.940
Hey!

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:31.700
I did it! I met Mew!

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.280
All the time I spent
with you all really helped!

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.700
Thank you!

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:45.460
But now,
I have a lot on my mind...

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:52.930
Dad!
Are Go and Satoshi here yet?

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:59.020
Satoshi hasn’t arrived yet,
but Go’s in the park.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.430
Okay, got it.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.310
You’re all going camping today, right?

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.610
Have fun!

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.690
We will, thank you!

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.190
Then should we wait
in the park, Eevee?

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.620
Which is why...

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.210
I’d like to go on a journey.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.880
But if I left to do that,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.500
I wouldn’t get to see all of you.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.210
And...

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.720
Eevee!

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.220
Koharu!

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.180
S-Sorry...

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.770
I wasn’t intending
to eavesdrop...

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.730
No, it’s fine.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.940
Go, what was that about
going on a journey...?

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:49.520
On my way back
from Project Mew,

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.230
I had a lot on my mind...

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.740
You can tell me
if you want.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:54.820
Right...

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.660
Meeting Mew
and becoming more fascinated by it...

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.500
It made me think I want to know more
about Mew, and get closer to Mew.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.620
And to do that...

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.130
I need to be a trainer
who can properly face up to Mew.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.130
A trainer who can face up to it?

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:15.050
I’m nowhere close to
good enough right now...

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.510
So, I had an idea.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:20.680
I thought I’d like to travel across
all sorts of regions, like Satoshi.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:21.890
So that’s why...

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.270
Yeah.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:28.230
If I leave Kuchiba City,
and meet lots more Pokémon and trainers,

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:31.730
and learn lots and lots more
about Pokémon and the world,

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:34.030
then I might be able to face up to Mew.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.110
So... you’d be going alone?

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:38.200
I’d end up relying on Satoshi
if he was there.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.320
So I’ll go alone.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.910
Have you told Satoshi?

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.290
Oh, he’d tell me to go for it.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.330
I know what he’s like.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:51.040
And... I feel kinda bad about it...

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.880
Like I’m betraying our friendship.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.220
So you don’t know what to do...

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.550
Oh, there you are!

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.550
Sorry I’m late!

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.890
Huh? Something wrong?

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.230
No, um... I...

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:51.870
Go!

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.330
Our promise!

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:02.010
“Next time we meet,
we’ll meet with a smile!” Right?

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.630
We did it!

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.260
I want to hear
how you beat Mr. Dande!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.560
And I wanna hear all about Mew!

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:09.520
Huh?

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.890
We’re about to miss the bus!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:40.090
This is the forest
my father took me to.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:41.670
Whoa...

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.270
It’s full of Pokémon!

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.560
Ooh! This place is great!

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:03.150
Right?
I <i>knew</i> you two would love it.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.030
The campsite is just up ahead.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:07.280
Tent, ready!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.700
Food, ready!

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.240
That just leaves...

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:12.870
Huh?

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:14.710
When did you...?

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.250
Where did you find those?

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:23.300
Let’s go find
enough for everyone.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:31.890
A Kamonegi!

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.100
It’s holding a plant stalk,

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.060
and it can swing it like a sword
to cut all sorts of things.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.570
It’s a Dugtrio!

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.450
It’s amazingly strong!
It can dig to a depth of 100 kilometers!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.490
You said the same thing
when we were little kids.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.330
Huh? Did I?

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:00.630
A Cayce!

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.880
Wow, they’re rare to see!

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:06.220
That brings back memories!

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:07.380
What memories?

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:07.970
So...

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:12.010
When I was younger,
I was often home alone.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:15.890
Once, when I was going through
my dad’s Pokémon Index...

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.950
Who are you?

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:36.950
After that, it started popping up
and vanishing every now and then.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:40.580
Then, one day...

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.930
You’re “Cayce,” right?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:09:00.270
You sleep for 18 hours a day,
and can even teleport in your sleep!

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:16.870
I thought it might’ve been teleporting
somewhere right nearby...

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:20.920
Are you home alone, too?

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.840
It was a sweltering day.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.990
I never knew there were
this many Pokémon in the park!

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.160
Cayce!

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:45.330
So Cayce was like a playmate for you
when you were home alone.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.130
Yeah.

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:49.340
And it led to me meeting
lots of Pokémon.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.510
Do you have any
memories like that, Satoshi?

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:55.220
Me? Hmm...

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.970
None that make me go,
“Ooh, it’s that Pokémon.”

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:58.930
Huh?

00:10:58.930 --> 00:10:59.930
You’re kidding, right?

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.980
If I had to say,
I guess I’d go with <i>all</i> the Pokémon I’ve met.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:08.980
After all, I wanna make friends
with every Pokémon!

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:12.070
Friends with all of them...
That’s amazing!

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.740
Oh, Momon Berries!

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.200
A Nyoromo?

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:43.560
Oh, no!

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:44.310
Not good!

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.600
Run for it!

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:57.700
A Yadon?!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.330
Yawn?

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.710
Eevee! Yawn!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.930
Good job, Eevee!

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.100
And thanks, Yadon!

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:36.240
<i>Pocket Monsters!</i>

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:02.760
Huh?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.010
What is it?

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.770
A Momon Berry...

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:07.770
Over there!

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.400
Maybe it’s thanking us
for saving it.

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.280
Huh? Do you think so?

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.870
Thank you, Nyoromo!

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:27.490
Satoshi and Pikachu
are a lot like one another.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.000
I think so, too.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.750
They’re both always charging ahead
and they have the same stubborn streak.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:38.340
Well, we’ve been
together for ages.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.680
Since I set out,
I’ve met lots of Pokémon...

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:46.390
I’ve helped them,
and they’ve helped me...

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:49.890
And there’s been times
I’ve said goodbye to them...

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:54.520
But Pikachu’s been by my side
since the beginning.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.610
He’s my number one partner.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:58.400
Your number one partner, huh?

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.030
You have a partner too, don’t you?

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.360
Huh? You mean this guy?

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:07.870
The first time it stood out to me...

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:11.660
That’d be seeing it
helping out its friends,

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.170
which made me think
I’d like to do the same.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:19.420
And traveling together,
I realized...

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.470
...that helping out your friends
is lots of fun!

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.470
And that friends are the best!

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:26.550
Yeah!

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:31.560
You always used to be all alone,
and said you didn’t need friends...

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.390
You’ve really changed.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.980
So have you, Koharu.

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.810
Huh? I have?

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.190
Yeah!

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:42.780
When we first met,
you didn’t like Pokémon...

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.990
...and just look at you now!

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:45.820
Yeah...

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.200
When I was lost, I met Eevee.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:55.500
Seeing Eevee’s evolutions,
and their bonds with their trainers...

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.290
...filled me with interest
in Pokémon!

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:04.010
So my world has expanded
thanks to Eevee.

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.260
I know that feeling!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.010
With Pokémon,
you can go anywhere!

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:13.520
With Pokémon,
you can connect with anyone in the world!

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:14.980
Yeah!

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:17.440
It sure is strange...

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:21.480
Catching Pokémon...
It feels like mere chance, but it’s not.

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:28.320
You mean it’s inevitable?
Or should I say, it’s destiny?

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.950
I don’t know about
all that complicated stuff,

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.160
but I’m glad we met.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.250
Thank you.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.290
I’ll say thanks, too!

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:38.210
Me, too... Thank you!

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:52.510
Satoshi.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.020
What’s wrong?

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:03.730
No, it’s nothing! Sorry.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:04.860
Okay.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:08.280
The stars sure are pretty tonight!

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.240
Go...

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.530
I’m going on a journey.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.580
I’ll be going on another journey,
with Pikachu.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:24.050
Going on a journey...
All of a sudden...

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:28.970
How could you decide that
without me?

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:30.260
Go...

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:34.970
Weren’t we friends?!

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.680
We’re <i>through!</i>

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:46.740
Go wasn’t sure
what he should do...

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.030
He wasn’t sure?

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:49.660
He wanted to go on a journey.

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:51.110
Huh? Go too?

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:54.120
But he couldn’t decide alone...

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:56.830
He said it was like
betraying your friendship...

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:03.130
Because you’re the first friend
Go’s ever had.

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:07.840
Go...

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.550
Hey! Go!

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:21.100
Calling... Calling... Calling...
Calling... Calli—

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:21.100
Go...

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:25.610
Incoming call from Koharu!
Incoming call from Koharu!

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:28.610
Incoming call from Koharu!

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.870
Calling... Calli—

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.250
What was that for?!

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:44.750
Huh? Pikachu!

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.000
It’s Trancell.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.790
They’re starting to evolve.

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.490
Will they be okay in the rain?

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:59.660
Butterfree scales repel water,
so they can even fly in the rain.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.910
That’s what the
Pokémon Index says, right?

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.290
Yeah.

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:12.340
Go...

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:13.170
Hold on!

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.340
I haven’t forgiven you just yet!

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.050
Forgiven me for what?

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:19.180
We’re still through, you know!
<i>Through!</i>

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:20.720
“Through”...
But you were going to—

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.180
You should ask me first!
I’ll miss you!

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:24.640
Ask you first?!

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.600
You were going to go alone too,
weren’t you?!

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:27.770
Huh?!

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:32.320
No, I... Wait, how do you know that...?
Koharu?!

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:41.740
What’s wrong?

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:46.580
This air flow, temperature,
humidity, altitude...

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.750
It might appear!

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.590
“It”?!

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:04.140
Lugia!

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:07.690
Why is it here?!

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:11.400
Lugia!

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:22.830
Does it want us to come?

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.660
Let’s go find out!

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.710
Hey, hold on!

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.670
Go! Satoshi!

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.670
Sheesh...

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.220
What are you planning to do?!

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:43.100
Battle it!

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.430
Battle Lugia?!

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:46.180
Of course!

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:50.020
Then I’ll catch it!

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.810
I’ll do it first!

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:15.750
Lucario, I choose you!

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:22.050
Inteleon, go!

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:32.060
Lugia, it’s a Raid Battle!

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:41.070
The Legendary Pokémon Lugia
suddenly appeared before Satoshi and Go.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.740
What will happen next?!

00:23:07.120 --> 00:23:09.580
Now, off to the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.990
Go!

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:12.370
Let’s go, everyone!

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:15.370
Pokémon really are...

00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:17.330
...awesome!

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:21.340
I wanna see more of them, know more about them,
make friends with more of them!

00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:26.800
The way that you go will determine
the Pokémon you’ll meet, and the adventures you’ll have.

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.390
And the choice is yours.

00:23:28.390 --> 00:23:30.260
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:33.680
Satoshi and Go!
A New Departure!!

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:36.770
Here we go!

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:38.860
Championing the evils of truth and love!

00:23:38.860 --> 00:23:40.520
Team Rocket Explorers!

00:23:41.360 --> 00:23:44.820
Following an order
to catch new Pokémon...

00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:47.660
...we made our first visit
to the Paldea Region.

00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:50.160
Oh, meow?
There’s one, meow!

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:52.620
It’s not in here!

00:23:52.620 --> 00:23:53.290
That means...

00:23:53.290 --> 00:23:55.000
...it’s a new species of Pokémon?!

00:23:57.830 --> 00:23:59.170
No, it’s not!

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:01.800
The Duckling Pokémon,
Kuwassu.

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:06.050
Its hair is slicked back
using a rich, moist cream?

00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:08.050
Sounds like Musashi, meow.

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:11.430
Let’s catch it quick;
what a great feeling that’ll be!

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:12.510
Yeah!

00:24:12.510 --> 00:24:13.930
<i>Go!</i>

00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:20.940
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:25.490
Today’s roundup-ssu!

